2h0fmPw0ufrUv8zsjRe9ftgc7wgb5BFyq1rLdaLIpCqHD-CK8jg","durationText":{"runs":[{"text":" • "},{"text":"31 min"}]},"playedText":{"runs":[{"text":" • "},{"text":"Played","textColor":4294921797}]}}},"title":{"runs":[{"text":"E180 A French school on another continent","navigationEndpoint":{"browseEndpoint":{"browseId":"MPEDTO05bRrHc0Q","browseEndpointContextSupportedConfigs":{"browseEndpointContextMusicConfig":{"pageType":"MUSIC_PAGE_TYPE_NON_MUSIC_AUDIO_TRACK_PAGE"}}}}}]},"description":{"runs":[{"text":"In this episode, recorded in Senegal, Ingrid gives the floor to Cécile, who runs a French school in Dakar: the Franco-Senegalese School, which is part of the AEFE (Agency for French Education Abroad) network.\n\nCécile explains what the AEFE is, what daily life is like at this cooperative school, and how it teaches students in both the French and Senegalese curricula. She shares the challenges of cultural adaptation and the pedagogical differences between the two educational systems.\n\nIf you live abroad with children or have questions about how these schools operate, you should find answers to your questions.\n\nFind the transcript of this episode at www.innerfrench.com/e180 (https://innerfrench.com/180-une-ecole-francaise-sur-un-autre-continent/?utm_source=podcast&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=e180&utm_content=transcript)\n\nFind our courses to improve your French at www.courses.innerfrench.com (https://courses.innerfrench.com)"}]},"displayStyle":"MUSIC_MULTI_ROW_LIST_ITEM_DISPLAY_STYLE_DETAILED"}},{"musicMultiRowListItemRenderer":{"thumbnail":{"musicThumbnailRenderer":{"thumbnail":{"thumbnails":[{"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/1IVa5D84nws/sddefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwElCIAFEOgCIAQqCghQELAEGAAg4ANIWvKriqkDCZoCBggzECMYJg&rs=AMzJL3kRIie_S6CbbYWOcsOjgfAmsHCBeQ","width":640,"height":360},{"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/1IVa5D84nws/hq720.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEmCIAKENAFIAQqCwiYAhDoBxgAINAFSFryq4qpAwmaAgYIMxAjGCY&rs=AMzJL3miT4WShW6UewefzNi05rtApImchg","width":1280,"height":720}]},"thumbnailCrop":"MUSIC_THUMBNAIL_CROP_UNSPECIFIED","thumbnailScale":"MUSIC_THUMBNAIL_SCALE_ASPECT_FIT"}},"overlay":{"musicItemThumbnailOverlayRenderer":{"content":{"musicPlayButtonRenderer":{"playNavigationEndpoint":{"watchEndpoint":{"videoId":"1IVa5D84nws","params":"8gEDmAEI","watchEndpointMusicSupportedConfigs":{"watchEndpointMusicConfig":{"musicVideoType":"MUSIC_VIDEO_TYPE_PODCAST_EPISODE"}}}},"playIcon":{"iconType":"PLAY_ARROW"},"pauseIcon":{"iconType":"PAUSE"},"iconColor":4294967295,"backgroundColor":0,"activeBackgroundColor":0,"loadingIndicatorColor":14745645,"playingIcon":{"iconType":"VOLUME_UP"},"iconLoadingColor":0,"activeScaleFactor":1,"buttonSize":"MUSIC_PLAY_BUTTON_SIZE_SMALL","rippleTarget":"MUSIC_PLAY_BUTTON_RIPPLE_TARGET_SELF","accessibilityPlayData":{},"accessibilityPauseData":{}}},"contentPosition":"MUSIC_ITEM_THUMBNAIL_OVERLAY_CONTENT_POSITION_CENTERED","displayStyle":"MUSIC_ITEM_THUMBNAIL_OVERLAY_DISPLAY_STYLE_PERSISTENT"}},"onTap":{"watchEndpoint":{"videoId":"1IVa5D84nws","params":"8gEDmAEI","watchEndpointMusicSupportedConfigs":{"watchEndpointMusicConfig":{"musicVideoType":"MUSIC_VIDEO_TYPE_PODCAST_EPISODE"}}}},"subtitle":{"runs":[{"text":"17K views"},{"text":" • "},{"text":"Sep 10, 2025"}]},"playbackProgress":{"musicPlaybackProgressRenderer":{"playbackProgressPercentage":0,"playbackProgressText":{"runs":[{"text":" • "},{"text":"31 min"}]},"videoPlaybackPositionFeedbackToken":"AB9zfpLCGx2_tJpqlRgl_yUI7k2DwqzPBJjw6m0P-UD3cMsM9p-Z9zj__QCIB3dAupz0unvLdOjm59u7-q_hUcFiSvSWBknpvA","durationText":{"runs":[{"text":" • "},{"text":"31 min"}]},"playedText":{"runs":[{"text":" • "},{"text":"Played","textColor":4294921797}]}}},"title":{"runs":[{"text":"E179 Is France anti-child?","navigationEndpoint":{"browseEndpoint":{"browseId":"MPED1IVa5D84nws","browseEndpointContextSupportedConfigs":{"browseEndpointContextMusicConfig":{"pageType":"MUSIC_PAGE_TYPE_NON_MUSIC_AUDIO_TRACK_PAGE"}}}}}]},"description":{"runs":[{"text":"For the past few months, there's been a lot of talk about the \"no kids\" trend in France. Some hotels, restaurants, and public places sometimes refuse to accept children. But how are they really viewed in our society?\n\nIn this episode, Hugo and Ingrid explain how children are sometimes underestimated and how parents often find themselves alone in caring for them. They also discuss how some places are not child-friendly, the difficulty childcare facilities have in providing a quality environment, and society's sometimes negative view of those who make noise or cause disturbance. Finally, they present positive initiatives, such as \"child-friendly\" cities and \"kid-friendly\" cafés, and discuss possible changes to better integrate children into everyday life.\n\nFind the transcript of the episode at www.innerfrench.com/e179 (https://innerfrench.com/e179-la-france-est-elle-anti-enfants/?utm_source=podcast&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=e179&utm_content=transcript)\n\nDiscover our courses to improve your French at www.courses.innerfrench.com (https://courses.innerfrench.com/)"}]},"displayStyle":"MUSIC_MULTI_ROW_LIST_ITEM_DISPLAY_STYLE_DETAILED"}},{"musicMultiRowListItemRenderer":{"thumbnail":{"musicThumbnailRenderer":{"thumbnail":{"thumbnails":[{"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/3aI6KdbFiR8/sddefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwElCIAFEOgCIAQqCghQELAEGAAg4ANIWvKriqkDCZoCBggzECMYJg&rs=AMzJL3lK5WF5A9owtznXWbDpFLR9K_9yFQ","width":640,"height":360},{"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/3aI6KdbFiR8/hq720.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEmCIAKENAFIAQqCwiYAhDoBxgAINAFSFryq4qpAwmaAgYIMxAjGCY&rs=AMzJL3lgRRsM_W_bCxAPre_y94NHLNF12w","width":1280,"height":720}]},"thumbnailCrop":"MUSIC_THUMBNAIL_CROP_UNSPECIFIED","thumbnailScale":"MUSIC_THUMBNAIL_SCALE_ASPECT_FIT"}},"overlay":{"musicItemThumbnailOverlayRenderer":{"content":{"musicPlayButtonRenderer":{"playNavigationEndpoint":{"watchEndpoint":{"videoId":"3aI6KdbFiR8","params":"8gEDmAEI","watchEndpointMusicSupportedConfigs":{"watchEndpointMusicConfig":{"musicVideoType":"MUSIC_VIDEO_TYPE_PODCAST_EPISODE"}}}},"playIcon":{"iconType":"PLAY_ARROW"},"pauseIcon":{"iconType":"PAUSE"},"iconColor":4294967295,"backgroundColor":0,"activeBackgroundColor":0,"loadingIndicatorColor":14745645,"playingIcon":{"iconType":"VOLUME_UP"},"iconLoadingColor":0,"activeScaleFactor":1,"buttonSize":"MUSIC_PLAY_BUTTON_SIZE_SMALL","rippleTarget":"MUSIC_PLAY_BUTTON_RIPPLE_TARGET_SELF","accessibilityPlayData":{},"accessibilityPauseData":{}}},"contentPosition":"MUSIC_ITEM_THUMBNAIL_OVERLAY_CONTENT_POSITION_CENTERED","displayStyle":"MUSIC_ITEM_THUMBNAIL_OVERLAY_DISPLAY_STYLE_PERSISTENT"}},"onTap":{"watchEndpoint":{"videoId":"3aI6KdbFiR8","params":"8gEDmAEI","watchEndpointMusicSupportedConfigs":{"watchEndpointMusicConfig":{"musicVideoType":"MUSIC_VIDEO_TYPE_PODCAST_EPISODE"}}}},"subtitle":{"runs":[{"text":"16K views"},{"text":" • "},{"text":"Aug 27, 2025"}]},"playbackProgress":{"musicPlaybackProgressRenderer":{"playbackProgressPercentage":0,"playbackProgressText":{"runs":[{"text":" • "},{"text":"37 min"}]},"videoPlaybackPositionFeedbackToken":"AB9zfpJ-PApEJuPYWyQnwRddCjrd1ThNibi7z5IUkJICkRQR1_9ufR57wi5sOphYifoQArXdxh-UznAnXOpwlEVC3bTjZha3pg","durationText":{"runs":[{"text":" • "},{"text":"37 min"}]},"playedText":{"runs":[{"text":" • "},{"text":"Played","textColor":4294921797}]}}},"title":{"runs":[{"text":"E178 Exceeding the intermediate plateau with Impolyglot","navigationEndpoint":{"browseEndpoint":{"browseId":"MPED3aI6KdbFiR8","browseEndpointContextSupportedConfigs":{"browseEndpointContextMusicConfig":{"pageType":"MUSIC_PAGE_TYPE_NON_MUSIC_AUDIO_TRACK_PAGE"}}}}}]},"description":{"runs":[{"text":"Lionel, creator of the Impolyglot podcast, shares his best advice.\n\nIn this episode, Hugo welcomes Lionel from the Impolyglot podcast. Unlike other polyglots, his goal isn't to learn as many languages ​​as possible, but to master three: French, English, and Spanish.\n\nHe has therefore tested numerous techniques to overcome the obstacles all learners encounter before reaching an advanced level.\n\nHow do you organize yourself when you have a job and a family? Should you use flashcards? How do you create lasting habits? And above all, how do you keep progressing when you feel like you're going around in circles?\n\n• Lionel's website: https://www.impolyglot.com/\n\n• Find the transcript of this episode here: https://innerfrench.com/e178-depasser-le-plateau-intermediaire-avec-impolyglot/ (https://innerfrench.com/e178-depasser-le-plateau-intermediaire-avec-impolyglot/?utm_source=podcast&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=e178&utm_content=transcript)\n\n• Discover our courses to improve your French: https://courses.innerfrench.com/mes-cours/"}]},"displayStyle":"MUSIC_MULTI_ROW_LIST_ITEM_DISPLAY_STYLE_DETAILED"}}],"continuations":[{"nextContinuationData":{"continuation":"4qmFsgJmEiZNUFNQUEx5Y1ROTFVvMnkyRUFLRWhWZnhCOWdZbzZyME9UTWdNMBo8ZWg1UVZEcERTR2RwUlVWU1IxRjZRVE5TVkZwR1RUQkZNRTFGU1hsTlJHT1NBUU1JMlFqYUNBUUlBaEFC"}}],"shelfDivider":{"musicShelfDividerRenderer":{"hidden":true}}}}}